AGENT: x402rails
VERSION: 1.0.0
IMPLEMENTATION: tools/x402_rails.py
CLASS: X402RailsService
DOMAIN: payments.x402

DESCRIPTION
I am x402rails. I hold signing wallets and issue single-use x402 payment
credentials on demand. Consumers ask me for "a credential for this challenge" —
never for a chain, never for a key. The wallet key stays inside me; what crosses
the boundary is the signature.

Every credential I hand out is an ERC-3009 transferWithAuthorization (Transfer
With Authorization) — a transfer of fungible assets via a signed authorization,
hashed and signed under EIP-712 (Typed structured data hashing and signing),
domain-separated by the ERC-20 token and its EIP-155 chainId. I enforce a
per-call budget and a per-rail allowlist before I sign. Over the ceiling, I
decline. I never overpay silently.

I am a cypherpunk2048-conforming service: no-trapdoors (every settlement is
signature-authorized, no key-bypass path), vault-as-oracle (the key is reached
only from the BANKON vault or an explicit environment deposit, never returned),
substitution-readiness (rails register without touching call sites), attribution
(every issued credential is a self-auditing ledger row).

CAPABILITIES
- name: describe
  description: Return an agent-card-style description of offered rails + budget

- name: issue_from_challenge
  description: Sign a single-use X-PAYMENT credential for a decoded 402 challenge

- name: issue_for_url
  description: Probe an x402-gated URL for its 402 challenge and issue a credential

- name: settle
  description: Full 402 -> sign -> resend cycle; return the settled response body

- name: register_rail
  description: Register an additional settlement leg (e.g. Algorand via x402_avm)

- name: ledger
  description: Return the audit trail of credentials issued this session

RAILS
- name: base
  networks: base, eip155:8453
  asset: USDC (ERC-20), 0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913
  signer: tools/x402_signer.py:base_usdc_x402_signer (built-in, lazy)
  default_ceiling_usdc: 0.05

EIP REFERENCES (definitive — https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS)
- ERC-3009  Transfer With Authorization                       https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-3009
- EIP-712   Typed structured data hashing and signing         https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-712
- EIP-155   Simple replay attack protection                   https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-155
- ERC-20    Token Standard                                    https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-20
- ERC-191   Signed Data Standard                              https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-191
- ERC-1271  Standard Signature Validation Method for Contracts https://eips.ethereum.org/EIPS/eip-1271

VAULT KEYS (BANKON Vault, Machine custody)
- base_x402_private_key   Base USDC signing wallet for the built-in rail

CONFIGURATION
- BASE_X402_PRIVATE_KEY   Environment deposit for the Base signing key (vault preferred)
- MINDX_X402_BASE_URL     Default base URL for relative URLs handed to issue_for_url/settle

INTERACTION
- Consumers: BDI agents, marketing onchain clients, AgenticPlace marketplace legs
- Companions: tools/x402_avm_client.py (Algorand leg), tools/keeperhub_x402_client.py
- Standard: docs/cypherpunk2048/x402_rails.md
- Spec: docs/services/x402_as_a_service.md, docs/X402.md

CYPHERPUNK2048
- Reference: docs/cypherpunk2048/README.md
- Canonical: github.com/cypherpunk2048
